### Fareground API examples
# Use the "REST Client" extension in VS Code (click "Send Request" above each
# block), or copy the bodies into Postman / Insomnia.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@token = paste-the-token-from-register-or-login-here

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Register a new player
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ada",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "walk1000steps"
}

### Log in
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "walk1000steps"
}

### Sync steps from an iPhone
# The Idempotency-Key makes a retry safe: send the SAME key when retrying a
# sync that timed out, and a FRESH one for a genuinely new batch of steps.
POST {{baseUrl}}/steps/sync
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

{
  "steps": 3500,
  "platform": "IOS",
  "deviceId": "iphone-demo-1"
}

### Sync steps from an Android phone
POST {{baseUrl}}/steps/sync
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

{
  "steps": 1200,
  "platform": "ANDROID",
  "deviceId": "pixel-demo-1"
}

### Replay the first sync - must NOT pay out again ("replayed": true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/steps/sync
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

{
  "steps": 3500,
  "platform": "IOS",
  "deviceId": "iphone-demo-1"
}

### An implausible claim - watch stepsAccepted and limit in the response
POST {{baseUrl}}/steps/sync
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "steps": 150000
}

### Ask for an attestation challenge (step 1 of App Attest / Play Integrity)
# Feed the returned nonce into DCAppAttestService (iOS) or the Play Integrity
# requestHash (Android), then send the result on the next /steps/sync.
POST {{baseUrl}}/attest/challenge
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sync with an attestation attached
# With ATTESTATION_MODE=off the verifier is skipped, but the nonce is still
# consumed - send this twice with the same nonce and the second returns 401.
POST {{baseUrl}}/steps/sync
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "steps": 500,
  "platform": "IOS",
  "deviceId": "iphone-demo-1",
  "attestation": {
    "token": "paste-the-base64-attestation-here",
    "nonce": "paste-the-nonce-from-attest-challenge-here"
  }
}

### Claim the square you are standing on (costs 100 WP)
POST {{baseUrl}}/parcels/claim
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "lat": 51.5129,
  "lng": -0.1471,
  "accuracyM": 6
}

### Claimed squares around a position (for the map)
GET {{baseUrl}}/parcels/nearby?lat=51.5129&lng=-0.1471&radius=300
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Everything you own
GET {{baseUrl}}/parcels
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Check balance (this is what credits passive coins)
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
